FR2-16 audit-2 verdict: FAIL
Core defect (GAP-101) only half-fixed: the "hides navigator.webdriver" half is now honest, but the
"Chrome-recommended stability flag" justification survives in packages/browser/README.md invariant #2,
packages/browser/src/launcher/browser-options.ts, and PROJECT_DEEP_DIVE.md s11.1 ("kept mainly as a
Chrome-recommended stability flag ... measured side effect"). Evidence it is false:
 - chromium-bad-flags-source.log: Chromium's bad_flags_prompt.cc lists --disable-blink-features in kBadFlags,
   commented "not supported and is intended only for use by Chromium developers".
 - webdriver-probe-audit2.log: via Sutradhar's real BrowserLauncher, the ONLY page-observable difference the
   flag makes (35 navigator props + window keys/chrome/plugins/langs/UA) is navigator.webdriver.
 - headed-infobar-probe.log + headed-chrome-window-cropped.png: with the flag present Chrome still shows
   "Chrome is being controlled by automated test software" -> contradicts "quiets some automation-related warnings".
 - puppeteer-core 25.5.0 defaults pass --enable-automation and do not include this flag.
So the webdriver effect is the flag's sole function, not a "side effect" of a stability flag.
